    {
      "Seq": 11,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 4010,
      "Actor": "Kenryc Greygate",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I find myself at noon in the heart of the village, tracks leading to the open dirt square, quarrying the open air for the heart of the place, patient as a hunter marking the run, sharp as a blade on the blade of my gaze. I mark the thorn hedge, square-craft row, where thorns set thick and pleached, turning stock. My attention sharpens on this quarry, ready to take. I mark the last track, let my focus go, and seek another run.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": "",
      "Phrase": "",
      "Lesson": false,
      "Attempt": "",
      "Succeeded": false
    },
    {
      "Seq": 12,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 4010,
      "Actor": "Kenryc Greygate",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I notice the thorn hedge, its thorns swelled and set thick, turning the stock as it pleaches. The scent of earth and thorn grows sharp, drawing me closer. I will examine this hedge by the plain ways of country folk, for it is at its best, ready for my careful scrutiny.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": "",
      "Phrase": "",
      "Lesson": false,
      "Attempt": "",
      "Succeeded": false
    },
    {
      "Seq": 13,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 4010,
      "Actor": "Kenryc Greygate",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I wish not to delve into the thorn hedge\u0027s thorns, for I seek to work, not to stand and watch. My hands yearn for the soil, not for idle thoughts.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": "",
      "Phrase": "",
      "Lesson": false,
      "Attempt": "",
      "Succeeded": false
    },
    {
      "Seq": 14,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 4010,
      "Actor": "Kenryc Greygate",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I will not linger on the thorn hedge, for it is too thorny and now is not its best time, drawing back to the calm of knowing when to move on. I can still examine the thorn hedge closely, another way. I will rely on the trapping and stalking of small game, for it is the time when these creatures are most accessible and their scent comes to its finest point, just before they slip away.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": "",
      "Phrase": "",
      "Lesson": false,
      "Attempt": "",
      "Succeeded": false
    },
